---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const title = 'Internal server error (500)';
const description = 'An unexpected server or network delivery condition interrupted your request on thevolumecalculator.com. Instructions to recover your session.';
const canonical = 'https://thevolumecalculator.com/500';
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | thevolumecalculator.com`}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  robots="noindex, follow"
>
  <Header />

  <main class="flex-1 max-w-4xl w-full mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8 sm:py-12 space-y-8 sm:space-y-10">
    <!-- Breadcrumb Navigation -->
    <nav class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-ink-muted">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-primary transition-colors">Home</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="text-ink font-semibold">500</span>
    </nav>

    <!-- Error Banner & Lead -->
    <section class="space-y-4">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold bg-white dark:bg-canvas-card border border-hairline text-accent-orange-deep shadow-xs">
        <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-accent-orange"></span>
        <span>HTTP status: 500</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-ink tracking-tight leading-tight">
        Internal server error
      </h1>

      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-ink-secondary leading-relaxed">
        Our network encountered an unexpected delivery interruption. While all mathematical calculations execute directly inside client browser memory, a network delivery error occurred while retrieving static assets from our Cloudflare edge distribution infrastructure. Edge caches synchronize across more than 300 data center facilities on the Cloudflare global network. Refreshing your browser tab in 5 seconds usually restores access. If this 500 error condition persists across multiple page reloads, please report the timestamp and your geographic region to <a href="mailto:contact@thevolumecalculator.com" class="text-primary font-semibold hover:underline">contact@thevolumecalculator.com</a> for immediate diagnostic inspection. Engineering monitors incident reports continuously.
      </p>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 pt-2">
        <a
          href="/"
          class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-xl bg-primary text-white text-xs sm:text-sm font-semibold hover:bg-primary-active transition-colors shadow-xs"
        >
          <span>Return to homepage</span>
        </a>
        <button
          onclick="window.location.reload()"
          class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-[#1e1e1e] border border-hairline text-ink text-xs sm:text-sm font-semibold hover:border-primary transition-colors shadow-xs cursor-pointer"
        >
          <span>Reload current page</span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Recovery Steps -->
    <section class="bg-white dark:bg-canvas-card rounded-2xl border border-hairline p-5 sm:p-7 shadow-xs space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight">
        System status and recovery instructions
      </h2>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-ink-secondary leading-relaxed">
        Three diagnostic steps appear below. First, perform a hard refresh by pressing Ctrl and F5 on Windows or Command, Shift, and R on macOS to bypass any stalled intermediate browser cache. Second, verify your local internet connection by pinging external DNS hosts like 1.1.1.1 or 8.8.8.8. Third, inspect the public Twitter status channel of Cloudflare or our maintainer profile on X at <a href="https://x.com/devxkamlesh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary font-semibold hover:underline">@devxkamlesh</a>. All code is open source. The GitHub repository preserves all 206 static page templates and 20 Vitest unit test suites, enabling developers to build and run the calculation suite locally on port 4321.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Contact & Assistance -->
    <section class="bg-white dark:bg-canvas-card rounded-2xl border border-hairline p-5 sm:p-7 shadow-xs space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-ink tracking-tight">
        Alternative access routes
      </h2>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-ink-secondary leading-relaxed">
        If you need direct volume conversions during an edge delivery interruption, you can review formulas and physical constants on our <a href="/methodology" class="text-primary font-semibold hover:underline">methodology</a> page or consult the <a href="/calculators" class="text-primary font-semibold hover:underline">all calculators</a> hub directory. For urgent questions, message our support inbox directly at <a href="mailto:contact@thevolumecalculator.com" class="text-primary font-semibold hover:underline">contact@thevolumecalculator.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
